# Game_SimonSays — Simon Says Memory (ID 4)
# Files: src/coordinator/Game_SimonSays.h, Game_SimonSays.cpp
# HTML: data/game_simon_setup.html, game_simon_names.html, game_simon_run.html

## GAMEPLAY
Classic memory pattern game. Computer shows color sequence, player repeats it.
Sequence grows by 1 each round. 1-3 groups with 3-4 pucks each.
Target: remember N-length sequence to win.

## CONFIG
- activeGroups (1-3), pucksPerGroup (default 4), targetSeqLength (default 15)
- speedSetting: 0=Slow(1200ms), 1=Med(800ms), 2=Fast(500ms)
- colorBlind, autoRestart, soundOn

## STATES per group
SIM_SETUP → SIM_READY → SIM_COUNTDOWN (3s) → SIM_SHOW → SIM_INPUT → SIM_FEEDBACK (1.5s) → loop
Terminal: SIM_FINISHED (rainbow) or SIM_FAIL (red, 5s)

## KEY MECHANICS
- Sequence stored as puck indices (0 to numPucks-1)
- SHOW: alternates color (full brightness, speed-dependent) and dim (25%)
- INPUT: per-puck debounce (same puck 400ms, different puck immediate), correct → advance, wrong → SIM_FAIL
- Complete sequence → FEEDBACK → add new color → SHOW again
- Reach targetSeqLength → SIM_FINISHED (rainbow on all pucks 2x)
- Stars counter tracks completed sequences
- 10 normal colors + 10 colorblind colors
- Team colors: Red, Blue, Yellow (group identifiers)

## COMMANDS
setup, cfg_groups, cfg_pucks_0/1/2, cfg_len, cfg_speed, cfg_blind, cfg_auto, cfg_sound,
start_all, start_X, stop_all, stop_X, exit

## STATUS JSON
{groups: [{state, len, step, stars, seq: ["#RRGGBB", ...]}]}
